WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.560
What has Melissa Rauch done to convince&nbsp;
her kids she's part of the judicial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.800
system? Her career went in a slightly different&nbsp;
direction after "The Big Bang Theory" ended.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:15.560
Melissa Rauch bid her character Dr. Bernadette&nbsp;
Rostenkowski-Wolowitz goodbye on "The Big Bang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.600
Theory" more than four years ago. With her&nbsp;
adorable facade and cut-throat actions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.480
Bernadette is one of the most intriguing "Big Bang&nbsp;
Theory" characters. Not only is the mother of two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.360
a brilliant scientist, but she also managed&nbsp;
something incredible: getting her husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.880
Simon Helberg's Howard Wolowitz, to suppress&nbsp;
his proclivity for being sleazy around women.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.400
Rauch also put on a cartoon-like voice when&nbsp;
portraying Bernadette. For this reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.880
it should come as no surprise that she has&nbsp;
been a successful voice actor following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.200
"The Big Bang Theory." Take a look at&nbsp;
her filmography and you'll see that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.320
the actor brought animated characters&nbsp;
to life for the kid-friendly shows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.400
"Firebuds" and "The Chicken Squad." In&nbsp;
addition, when she is not in a recording studio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.000
Rauch puts on her executive producer hat for&nbsp;
the "Night Court" reboot. She also has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.120
showing off her comedy skills as the show's&nbsp;
protagonist, Judge Abracadabra "Abby" Stone.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.040
Rauch discussed the "Night Court"&nbsp;
reboot in a February 2023 interview&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.840
on the "Jennifer Hudson Show." The New&nbsp;
Jersey native shared that she believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.040
those unfamiliar with the comedy's source&nbsp;
material would like the new show just as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.800
much as hardcore fans. She hinted that&nbsp;
her character inherited her father's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.640
inability to hide his whimsy, even while&nbsp;
wearing his judge robe. The actor shared,

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.000
"What I love about it is that people&nbsp;
who loved the original incarnation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.520
there's so much for them that they&nbsp;
will remember and nostalgia and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.680
just all these little Easter eggs that&nbsp;
they will remember from the original."

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.720
"And then for people who don't have any prior&nbsp;
knowledge of it, they can come into it with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.960
fresh eyes and they don't need to have,&nbsp;
you know, that familiarity with it either."

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.480
While Rauch clearly takes pride in her work,&nbsp;
it seems that her children might not be quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:54.560
as enthusiastic about her job. Even though her&nbsp;
kids, Brooks and Sadie, may have enjoyed a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.360
episodes of "Firebuds" and "The Chicken Squad,"&nbsp;
it's unlikely they are that aware their mother is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.160
an actor on the animated shows. While speaking to&nbsp;
Hudson, the "Big Bang Theory" star explained that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.520
her son and daughter are under the impression&nbsp;
that she actually works in a court of law.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.784
"Is it wrong that I haven't corrected them?"

00:02:10.784 --> 00:02:12.960
"No you can keep it in your back pocket."

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.400
"They've seen the posters for it and they're&nbsp;
like, 'Mom's a judge!' And I'm like, 'Yes, I am.'"

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:22.360
During a February 2023 appearance on "The View,"&nbsp;
Rauch shared that there have been some tricky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:26.480
aspects about appearing in "Night Court." She&nbsp;
noted that some "Big Bang Theory" viewers may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:32.160
find watching the 2023 sitcom jarring because she&nbsp;
did not change her natural voice. The actor joked,

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.720
"I don't tend to read a lot of Instagram&nbsp;
comments but I did notice that people were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.320
concerned that I wasn't using the same&nbsp;
voice that I use for Bernadette on 'Big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.840
Bang.' The reaction is a little bit&nbsp;
like when you are transitioning from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:47.734
silent movies into talkies. Like people are&nbsp;
horrified that I'm not talking like that."

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.880
However, Rauch does not seem to&nbsp;
mind being associated with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.800
"Big Bang Theory" character. The actor&nbsp;
helped contribute to the 2022 book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:59.000
"The Big Bang Theory: The Definitive,&nbsp;
Inside Story of the Epic Hit Series."

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.040
During an October 2022 interview with the book's&nbsp;
author, Jessica Radloff, Rauch shared that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:09.320
missed the CBS comedy for several reasons. She&nbsp;
noted that she longed for the days that she could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.600
regularly interact with "The Big Bang Theory"&nbsp;
cast and crew — but it's not just her coworkers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.280
she missed. She apparently was also very fond&nbsp;
of the omelet bar that was set up for the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:24.575
stars once a week. Either way, it seems she has as&nbsp;
much love for her time on the show as her fans do.

